Symptom:
The customer is experiencing repeated MFA prompts on Microsoft Entra joined AVD machines when accessing banking websites. This issue does not occur on Domain joined machines.
Cause:
The root cause appears to be related to third-party websites, as confirmed by a collaboration engineer. The issue persists despite various troubleshooting steps, indicating that it may not be directly related to the AVD environment itself.

Action plan:

Configuring the registry key:
 
HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\Software\Policies\Microsoft\AzureADAccount
Value Name: LoadCredKeyFromProfile
Type: REG_DWORD
Data: 1
 
enables a specific behavior in Azure Virtual Desktop (AVD) or FSLogix environments that use Microsoft Entra ID (formerly Azure AD).

What This Setting Does
Setting LoadCredKeyFromProfile to 1 allows the system to load the user's credential key from their profile during login. This is particularly useful in non-persistent environments like AVD, where:
	• User profiles are stored in FSLogix containers (e.g., VHD/VHDX files).
	• Without this setting, browser cookies, saved passwords, and other credentials may be lost after a reboot or session reset.
	• Enabling this ensures credential continuity across sessions 
	
When to Use It
	• You're using FSLogix profile containers with Microsoft Entra ID (cloud-only or hybrid).
	• You want to preserve user credentials (like browser logins) across sessions.
	• You're deploying Azure Virtual Desktop or similar VDI solutions.
	
 Important Notes
	• This setting does not apply to traditional Active Directory environments.
	• It may interact with security features like Credential Guard, so test thoroughly in your environment.
	• Ensure that FSLogix and Entra ID integration is properly configured.
